.DS_Store

# Bytecode caches. Python writes one beside the module it imports, so several trees
# in this repository carry a copy and any test run rewrites them: a tracked cache
# is a working tree that dirties itself, holding bytes that describe the
# interpreter which produced them rather than anything this repository decided.
# The rule sits at the root because only a root pattern reaches every tree; an
# ignore file inside one toolchain cannot see past its own directory.
#
# One cache, under tools/conver/siprs-with-4layers/, stays tracked. That tree is
# the frozen answer key and tests assert nothing writes into it, so a rewrite there
# is a finding rather than dirt. An ignore rule never applies to a tracked file, so
# this rule leaves that one exactly as it was.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

